{{PageImage|XP.png}}
'''Level-up''' is a feature that allows players to spend XP to improve [[Cat Units]] and Base Upgrades. Level upgrades can be done by entering the [[Upgrade Menu]], scrolling to the desired Cat Unit or Base Upgrade and pressing the "Upgrade!" button.

==Explanation==
All Cat Units and Base Upgrades start at level 1. Each upgrade increases the level by 1. Levelling up a Cat Unit will increase its health and attack power, while levelling up a Base Upgrade will make it more effective (e.g. levelling up the Study upgrade increases amount of XP earned after [[Battle|battle]]). Every level-up will also raise the player's [[User Rank]] by 1 level. There is a limit to how many times a unit may be upgraded. The level cap is initially 10, but it can be increased all the way up to 50 for most units (60 for [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|ubers]]) as the player raises their User Rank and progresses through the game.

The XP costs will increase with each upgrade until level 10, at which point they will become multiples of the first 10 levels' costs. These specific multiples are 2 for levels 11-20, 3 for 21-30, and then adds 0.5 to the multiplier every 10 levels after that (so that would be 3.5 for 31-40, 4 for 41-50, 4.5 for 51-60, and beyond, despite no cats being upgradeable past 60). This pattern continues all the way up to the cat's maximum natural level; [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline]] is the only cat to break the pattern and always costs 999,999 for each level.

In addition to standard levels (also known as natural or XP levels), many units can also upgrade to '''plus levels''' (also known as '''+ levels'''). Each plus level is equivalent to a natural level, but the limits for plus levels are different: for example [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] can be upgraded to level 20 by using XP, but with plus levels its true level cap is 20+90. Plus levels are attained by "using" duplicate Cat Units or Ability Capsules in Cat Storage. As a result, only cats obtainable from gacha (including [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[Lucky Capsule|Lucky]] and [[:Category:Gacha Cats|Rare]] capsules) can be upgraded to plus levels.

Levelling up Cat Units can also unlock new forms and abilities: upgrading any Cat Unit to total level 10 will unlock its Evolved Form, and upgrading a Normal Cat to total level 30 (i.e. 20+10) will unlock its [[True Form]]. Other Cats have a minimum level and additional requirements that must be met before their True Forms can be unlocked (20 for [[:Category:Cats requiring Awakening for True Form|cats needing Awakening]]; 30 for [[:Category:Cats requiring Catfruits for True Form|cats needing Catfruit]]). Additionally, certain Uber Rare Cats can unlock [[Ultra Form]]s upon reaching level 60.

During certain [[Million Downloads Event]]s, a "Half XP Cost Event" will appear on Friday, Saturday and Sunday for a few weeks. It halves the XP costs for upgrading all Cat Units and the amount of XP needed to evolve units.

