Below are examples using the simple equation for [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]]'s HP at level 20, 25 and 40 with maximum [[Main Chapters Levels#Legendary Cat Shield|Legendary Cat Shield]] activated.

<math>\text{Stats at level }20 = \Bigl\lfloor \operatorname{round}\left(450 \times \frac{24}{5}\right) \times 2.5 \Bigr\rfloor = 5,400 \text{ HP}</math><br>
<sup>Here, Treasure Bonus Multiplier = 2.5, Initial Stat = 450, and (n+4) = (20+4) = 24.</sup>

<math>\text{Stats at level }25 = \Bigl\lfloor \operatorname{round}\left(450 \times \frac{29}{5}\right) \times 2.5 \Bigr\rfloor = 6,525 \text{ HP}</math><br>
<sup>Here, Treasure Bonus Multiplier = 2.5, Initial Stat = 450, and (n+4) = (25+4) = 29.</sup>

<math>\text{Stats at level }40 = \Bigl\lfloor \operatorname{round}\left(450 \times \frac{44}{5}\right) \times 2.5 \Bigr\rfloor = 9,900 \text{ HP}</math><br>
<sup>Here, Treasure Bonus Multiplier = 2.5, Initial Stat = 450, and (n+4) = (40+4) = 44.</sup>

Below are examples for calculating [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]'s HP at level 25, 75 and 95, to showcase how to calculate the stats of a unit that surpasses 1st and/or 2nd reduction point, with maximum [[Main Chapters Levels#Legendary Cat Shield|Legendary Cat Shield]] activated.

<math>\text{Stats at level }25 = \Bigl\lfloor \operatorname{round}\left(1050 \times \frac{29}{5}\right) \times 2.5 \Bigr\rfloor = 15,225 \text{ HP}</math><br>
<sup>Here, Treasure Bonus Multiplier = 2.5, Initial Stat = 1050, m = 70, p = 90, and (n+4) = (25+4) = 29.</sup>

<math>\text{Stats at level }75 = \Bigl\lfloor \operatorname{round}\left(1050 \times \left(\frac{74}{5} + \frac{5}{10}\right)\right) \times 2.5 \Bigr\rfloor = 40,162 \text{ HP}</math><br>
<sup>Here, Treasure Bonus Multiplier = 2.5, Initial Stat = 1050, m = 70, p = 90, and (n+4) = 74 which is greater than m, therefore (m+4) = 74 and (n-m) = 5.</sup>

<math>\text{Stats at level }95 = \Bigl\lfloor \operatorname{round}\left(1050 \times \left(\frac{74}{5} + \frac{20}{10} + \frac{5}{20}\right)\right) \times 2.5 \Bigr\rfloor = 44,757 \text{ HP}</math><br>
<sup>Here, Treasure Bonus = 2.5, Initial Stat = 1050, (n-1) = 94 which is higher than p, therefore (m+4) = 74, (p-m) = 20, and (n-p) = 5.</sup>

==Effect on Base Upgrades==
*Cat Cannon Power - Increases [[Cat Cannon]] attack power by 50 and Cat Cannon recharge time by 50 frames per level.
*Cat Cannon Range - Increases Cat Cannon attack range. It starts at 3 Cannon waves (different that regular [[Wave Attack|waves]]) and increases by 1 per level.
*Cat Cannon Charge - Decreases Cat Cannon recharge time by 50 frames per level.
*Worker Cat Rate - Increases the rate of income by 3¢ per second per level.
*Worker Cat Wallet - Increases the [[Worker Cat]]'s wallet, increasing upper limit of income. Adds 100 starting wallet per level, +50 per Worker Cat level while in the stage.
*Base Defense - Increases the health of the [[Cat Base]] by 1,000 HP per level.
*Research - decreases Cat recharge time. It has no effect at level 1, but from level 2 and after, recharge time will be decreased by 0.2 seconds (at level 20+10, the recharge time is decreased by 5.8 seconds).
*Accountant - Increases the money earned when an enemy is defeated. It has no effect at level 1, but from level 2 and after, money earned from enemies will be increased by 5% (at level 20+10, the money drop from enemies is increased by 145%).
*Study - Increases the amount of XP received when clearing a stage. It has no effect at level 1, but from level 2 and after, XP will be increased by 5% (at level 20+10, the XP received when clearing a stage is increased by 145%).
*Cat Energy - Increases the limit of [[Cat Energy]] by 10 per level.

==Trivia==
*[[The Cat God (Special Cat)|The Cat God]] and [[Cheetah Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cheetah Cat]] are the only characters in the [[Upgrade Menu]] that can't be leveled up through any means.
*[[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] are the only cats that evolve into their True Form automatically by leveling up.

